<Concept title="Trap counterplay and recovery" section="States">
  <p>This contract covers issues #94, #738, #724, #737, #592, #341,
  #345, #473 and the repeat-completion portion of #62. It defines the remake
  behavior exercised by this batch; it does not claim complete original parity.</p>
  <h2>Inventory and recovery</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Each character MUST save inventory order as an explicit ordered list of
    item IDs alongside quantities. JSON key sorting MUST NOT change manual order.
    Unknown/duplicate order entries MUST be ignored; unlisted items MUST be retained.
    Legacy saves without a list MUST retain their available dictionary order.</li>
    <li>On a lethal field hit, one held Scape Doll MUST be consumed before defeat
    is emitted. The player MUST reach zero HP, fall down and remain down under a
    red screen wash before revival particles play. Only after the particle phase
    MUST HP become full and the stand-up animation begin. Harmful statuses MUST
    clear; the encounter and meseta MUST remain unchanged. Input and damage MUST
    remain blocked throughout, with two seconds of recovery immunity from stand-up
    (remake tuning). The return-to-city prompt MUST NOT appear.
    Without a doll the existing defeat transaction MUST run exactly once.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Trap counterplay</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Dormant field balls MUST be visible and attackable to CASTs and to characters
    with Trap Vision. Arming MUST reveal the ball to everybody. Hidden balls MUST
    NOT steal targeting or projectile hits. Revealed hostile balls MUST disarm on
    a damaging weapon contact, without detonating or awarding enemy EXP/drops.</li>
    <li>Player traps MUST NOT be treated as enemies. Multiple player traps MAY be live simultaneously:
    placing another MUST NOT expire or detonate previously placed traps. Placement MUST be
    refused without consumption outside a field, by non-CASTs, or while defeated.</li>
    <li>Trap Vision retains the existing 60-second wall-clock duration and refreshes
    to the later expiry; it MUST survive room changes but MUST reset when changing
    characters, starting a fresh expedition, ending/resetting a session, or dying. City/dead use MUST NOT consume it.
    The inventory MUST offer Use for Trap Vision and report its 60-second duration
    after activation; city use MUST explain the field-only restriction. Supported
    trap items MUST offer Use to CASTs, and Sol Atomizer MUST offer Use. Scape Dolls
    remain automatic and MUST NOT offer manual Use.
    These duration/scope choices are remake rules, not recovered PSZ measurements.</li>
    <li>A hostile trap contact MUST resolve damage and status under the same dodge,
    recovery and defeat guards. Healing MUST NOT revive a defeated player.
    A spent/disarmed trap MUST NOT trigger or apply its payload twice.</li>
    <li>Trigger range and blast range MUST be represented separately. This batch
    retains 4-unit hostile radii as remake tuning. The subsequent
    <a href={siteUrl('/states/trap-validation')}>trap-validation contract</a> replaces the 60 Hz fuse divisor with a
    live-traced 30 Hz timebase and separates rise from countdown. Original
    hostile radii and Light Trap confusion remain #607/#724 research work; the existing stun substitute MUST remain labelled as such.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Status delivery and support</h2>
  <p>The 3D player MUST accept the currently supported trap payloads: freeze,
  burn and the temporary stun substitute. Existing project duration/potency values
  are used, not newly asserted original-game numbers. Duplicate effects MUST NOT
  stack or refresh. Burn ticks MUST use elapsed gameplay time and stop on cure,
  death or expiry. Once inflicted, burn MUST NOT be dodged and MUST NOT interrupt
  movement or break freeze. Anti MUST clear player ailments; Resta MUST heal the living
  player, using the learned level and the existing support power table. CAST
  characters MUST NOT cast through stale palette entries. Neither support cast may emit the offensive fallback fire projectile.
  Reverser and the still-unimplemented 3D buffs/debuffs (Shifta, Deband, Jellen,
  Zalure) MUST reject the cast without spending PP and show feedback. They remain
  follow-up work in #345.</p>
  <p>Sol Atomizer MUST cure the living field player's active ailments and consume
  one item only when there is an ailment to cure. It MUST NOT restore HP. A Moon
  Atomizer without a supported downed teammate MUST be rejected without consumption;
  it MUST NOT act as a full self-heal. Companion revival remains follow-up work.</p>
  <h2>Rendering and boss completion</h2>
  <p>Bear and needle traps MUST use instance-owned materials with the source-derived
  profiles in <a href={siteUrl('/states/trap-validation')}>trap validation</a>, including each
  surface's scale, translation and repeat/mirror bits. Off MUST hide only the
  animated prongs/spikes. Bear release and scene teardown MUST release the player
  hold without overwriting damage, defeat or revival state. Armed prongs MUST scroll.
  Original floor animation timing remains unmeasured; the static texture
  transforms supersede the earlier storybook tuning.</p>
  <p>Repeated room-clear checks MUST NOT create multiple boss return warps. Objective
  updates after the fight MUST still be able to unlock a deferred exit.</p>
  <p>Dialog boxes MUST own a copy of their page array; closing a dialog MUST NOT
  clear the caller's constant/read-only data. This regression was observed during
  the field-entry matrix and is covered by the seeded test.</p>
  <h2>Verification</h2>
  <p>Seeded test-runner cases cover save reconstruction, recovery guards and trap
  state boundaries. The gameplay batch probe exercises real actors/materials,
  hurtbox contacts and support delivery. Human playtesting covers visual quality,
  trap readability and full boss runs; passing logic checks does not close those gaps.</p>
  <h2>Manual confirmation: multiple traps and Scape Doll revival</h2>
  <p>Use a CAST with at least two trap items, and a non-CAST with Trap Vision.
  Carry two Scape Dolls for the revival checks. Run these checks in a field.</p>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Multiple traps:</strong> place one trap away from enemies, move a
    few steps, then place another. Both MUST remain present. Lure enemies into
    each and confirm each trap can trigger independently. Each placement consumes
    one item; placing the second MUST NOT detonate or remove the first.</li>
    <li><strong>Timed Trap Vision:</strong> as a non-CAST, use Trap Vision near a
    hidden, dormant trap. It MUST become visible and targetable. Move to another
    room before 60 seconds elapse: reveal MUST carry over, but room entry MUST NOT
    restart the timer. After 60 seconds from use, dormant traps MUST be hidden
    and untargetable again. CAST visibility remains available without the item.</li>
    <li><strong>Visible death:</strong> with two dolls held, take a lethal hit.
    HP MUST show zero, the player MUST fall and lie down, and the play area MUST
    turn red while the HUD remains readable. There MUST be no return-to-city prompt.</li>
    <li><strong>Revival:</strong> gold particles MUST rise around the fallen player
    before HP refills. The player MUST then stand up, the red wash MUST fade, and
    movement/attacks MUST resume after recovery. Exactly one doll is consumed;
    active ailments clear, meseta remains unchanged, and the encounter continues.</li>
    <li><strong>Repeated hits:</strong> repeat while surrounded by enemies. Hits
    during the fall, particle phase and two-second stand-up recovery MUST NOT
    interrupt revival or consume the second doll. Controls MUST NOT bypass recovery.</li>
    <li><strong>Without a doll:</strong> remove remaining dolls and take a lethal
    hit. Normal defeat and the return-to-city prompt MUST still work.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>Record any failure with the character class, room, item counts before/after,
  and a short clip if animation order, screen tint or controls feel wrong.</p>
</Concept>
